The attached image demonstrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances antigen-specific antibody responses, comparable to or exceeding aluminum hydroxide (AH) adjuvant. Box plots show anti-rPA IgG titers in mice immunized with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) alone, or rPA combined with varying doses of AH or Nano-11. Both adjuvants significantly increased antibody titers compared to rPA alone. Notably, at lower doses like 12.5 µg, Nano-11 maintained strong adjuvanticity, whereas AH showed a diminished effect. This highlights Nano-11's potent immunopotentiating effect and potential as an effective vaccine adjuvant.